  "name": "Immolate",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-creature-skeleton.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Flames wreathe one creature you can see within range. The target must make a Dexterity saving throw. It takes 9d6 fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. On a failed save, the target also burns for the creation’s duration.\nThe burning target sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the saving throw. It takes 3d6 fire damage on a failed save, and the creation ends on a successful one. These flames can’t be extinguished by anything less than a creation.\nIf damage from this creation reduces a target to 0 hit points, the target is turned to ash.</p>",
